{
  "id": "pokemon-card-game-players-club",
  "name": "Pokémon Card Game Players Club",
  "category": "program",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Card Game Players Club, launched in Japan in January 2003 as the successor of the Pokémon Card Fan Club, gave its members EXP points for playing in official events and weekly leagues, and promo cards for joining, renewing and earning EXP. Its promos are numbered PLAY and carry the club's red P in place of the promo star. These are the joining, renewal and event cards; the EXP cards are under Pokémon Card Game Players Club EXP.\n\nMembers who joined for the first season, 2003, received cosmos holo Regice ex, Regirock ex and Registeel ex. New members in 2004 got the three legendary birds, Moltres ex, Articuno ex and Zapdos ex, and renewing members a sealed pack of nine: the birds, the owner's Celebi, Mew and Jirachi, whose names have a blank for the player to write their own, and Cyclone, Boost and Warp Energy. The 2005 pack, for new and renewing members alike, swapped the birds for the owner's Kyogre, Groudon and Rayquaza, and members renewing in 2006 got a kit of seven with Ho-Oh ex, Lugia ex and Jirachi ex. Members also got Pokémon Card Fan at Battle Road Summer 2003 and Master Ball at Battle Road Spring 2004. The club's fifth season, 2007, was its last.",
